{title: Jesus Paid It All}
{lyricist: Elvina M. Hall}
{composer: John T. Grape}
{year: 1865}
{meta: tune-year 1868}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune ALL TO CHRIST}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to ALL TO CHRIST}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags cross, atonement}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [D]hear the Savior [G]say,
"Thy [D]strength indeed is [A]small;
[D]Child of weakness, [G]watch and pray,
[D]Find in [A]Me thine [D]all in all."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Jesus paid it [G]all,
[D]All to Him I [A]owe;
[D]Sin had left a [G]crimson stain,
He [D]washed it [A]white as [D]snow.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Lord, now indeed I [G]find
Thy [D]power, and Thine a[A]lone,
[D]Can change the [G]leper's spots
And [D]melt the [A]heart of [D]stone.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
For [D]nothing good have [G]I
Where[D]by Thy grace to [A]claim;
I'll [D]wash my [G]garments white
In the [D]blood of [A]Calvary's [D]Lamb.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
And [D]when, before the [G]throne,
I [D]stand in Him com[A]plete,
"[D]Jesus died my [G]soul to save,"
My [D]lips shall [A]still re[D]peat.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
